{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"4a573e7bfd1e047000fc3b0335a4fb147a9e64145b43ec960122d6393dbfdf03","digest":{"component_or_area":"build/lint infrastructure","key_entities":["scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py","Makefile","lint target","tests/unit/test_comment_hygiene_guard.py",".github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml","scripts/gen_env_registry.py","tests/unit/test_config_gate_wiring_heldout.py"],"problem_keywords":["comment-hygiene","gate wiring","make lint","local verification","ci-local mismatch"],"propositions":["The comment-hygiene gate runs in CI as a standalone step but is not wired into `make lint`, causing local verification to pass while CI rejects the same changes.","Running `make lint` locally does not catch comment-hygiene violations that CI detects, wasting review cycles and forcing unnecessary CI re-runs.","The comment-hygiene gate should be added to the `make lint` target alongside the existing `gen_env_registry.py --check` gate, following the documented drift-gate precedent.","The wiring must be verified by a test assertion in `test_comment_hygiene_guard.py` that confirms the lint target invokes the script, with a teeth case proving the assertion fails when the invocation is removed."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787901455512229001,"uuid":"ba8e5094-54b9-488c-aac4-51d3e079ece5"}